                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>At a meeting of the Allied High Commission on December 15 and 16, François-Poncet
                    again reported the agreement of his government to the recommendations of October
                    27 on the political status of Berlin, this time without mentioning any
                    reservations. The High Commissioners, however, agreed not to take any action on
                    the recommendations until the Berlin Magistrat presented its draft constitution
                    in early January. (Telegram 66, December 17, from Bonn, not printed, 740.0019
                    Control (Germany)/12–1749)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
